special_abilities:
  - name: "Lemurian R.C.C. Abilities"
    description: "The Sea Sentinel keeps everything the Lemurian race has; see the Lemurian for the full rules. Life Sense: 25 foot (7.6 m) radius plus 5 feet (1.5 m) per level, and 20% +5% per level to locate, track or find a specific type of animal or plant, +5% underwater. Empathy with Animals: an automatic affinity with animals of all kinds except monsters, predators and sentient creatures. Ley Line Powers: heals and recovers P.P.E. twice as fast as a normal human on a ley line or at stone pyramids, and swims 25% faster along ley lines. Natural Abilities: as all Lemurians. Pets and Familiars: may be accompanied by an Aquatic Lemur or other pet, and some have a personal riding animal (player''s choice). Ultrasonic Communication: range 2,000 feet (610 m) underwater, 400 feet (122 m) on the surface or in the air."
  - name: "Born to Soar"
    description: "Can pilot any aircraft or submersible. In any Lemurian stone vehicle, submersible or Stone Flyer the base skill is 80% +2% per level, with +1 attack/action per melee round, +2 on initiative and +2 to automatic dodge. The usual penalties for aerial acrobatics, dog fighting, evasive action and trick maneuvers are halved to begin with, and then lessened by a further 1% per level of the pilot''s experience. The same training lets the Sea Sentinel fly any human, D-Bee or alien aircraft, submersible, amphibious vehicle or suit of power armor with air or underwater capability, but in technology-based machines not made of stone or powered by magic the piloting skill is at -15%, all the standard trick maneuver penalties apply in full, and the pilot is -1 attack per melee round."
  - name: "Machine Awareness"
    description: "Much like a Cyber-Knight''s Zen Combat, the Sea Sentinel feels the combat vehicle and every mechanical device and tech-weapon used by one specific opponent whenever it targets or tracks him: targeting, radar and tracking systems, Vibro-Blades, Neural Maces, handheld guns, and the weapons built into body armor, power armor, cyborgs, robots and combat vehicles - any combat machine with moving parts, electricity or a computer chip. He knows the instant a targeting computer or radar locks on, a trigger is about to be squeezed, an energy cell charges, a cybernetic muscle tenses or a turret begins to aim. Effects: negates any bonuses the attacker has from the weapon, machine or targeting device he is operating; +1 on Perception Rolls involving machines and technology; +1 on initiative and +1 to automatic dodge against manned guns, weapon systems and machines (bionics, power armor, vehicular weapon systems), doubled against automated attackers such as artificial intelligences, computers, unmanned robots like Skelebots and automated defense systems. At level one he can focus on only one opponent and that opponent''s weapons; the number of opponents he can sense and react to rises by one at levels 4, 8 and 12. He also senses when a robot or automated optic system is targeting, watching, videotaping or following him - he may not locate a well hidden device, but he knows it is there."
  - name: "Ley Line Powers"
    description: "No spell casting, but a few magic abilities tied to the fighter pilot''s work. Speed: along a ley line, increases the speed of any Lemurian stone aircraft, submersible or amphibious vehicle by 50% without strain or damage to the vehicle; man-made tech vehicles gain only 10%. Weapon range: weapons built into Lemurian vehicles gain 5% range per level of experience; not applicable to man-made tech vehicles. Weapon damage: +1D6 damage on a ley line (or as stated under the specific weapon system). Force field: once every six hours, and only while traveling along a ley line, erect a magical force field around the vessel with 2D6+10 M.D.C. per level of experience, lasting ten minutes per level or until reduced to zero M.D.C. Miracle crash landing: on or within two miles (3.2 km) of a ley line the vehicle takes the entire force and all the damage of a crash landing, and the pilot and any passengers walk away unscathed."
  - name: "O.C.C. Psionics and Intuitive Machine Operations"
    description: "Every Sea Sentinel develops Empathy (4), Machine Ghost (12), Meditation (0), Mind Block (4), Object Read (6), Sense Time (2), Telemechanics (10), Telemechanic Mental Operation (12) and Telepathy (4), which let him understand and use the machines and technology of other people. I.S.P. is 2D4x10 plus the M.E. attribute number, +2D4 per level of experience. Considered a Major Psychic. No other psionics are available to this character."
trackable_resources:
  - { key: ley-line-force-field, label: "Ley Line Force Field", max: 1, reset_on: never, note: "Once per every six hours, only while traveling along a ley line. 2D6+10 M.D.C. per level; lasts ten minutes per level." }
restrictions:
  - "Race: exclusive to the Lemurians; no other race is permitted."
  - "Alignment: any, though most are Principled (20%), Scrupulous (40%), Unprincipled (20%) or Anarchist (10%)."
  - "A high M.E. is suggested, but not a necessity."
  - "Psionics: the nine listed powers only. No other psionics are available to this character."
  - "Cybernetics: none. Lemurians have no interest in bionics, not even Bio-Systems."
  - "Combat vehicle: every Sea Sentinel is assigned a Sea Dart Interceptor, and can be assigned different vehicles depending on the mission and the vessels available. The page lists the Sea Dart Interceptor under Standard Equipment as an assigned vehicle, and it is a vehicle row here rather than a gear item."
  - "Also has access to all Bio-Skins. Special or additional vehicles, weapons and gear may be assigned for special situations and missions."
  - "Money: a monthly salary of 2,300 credits or trade goods, double for squadron leaders; starts with one month''s pay. Even low ranking Sea Sentinels often have a spacious apartment or family home in one of the floating cities, and there are barracks for long duty - each with room for three Sea Sentinels, a lavatory, a sitting room, a study and a small kitchen."
  - "Related skills the list cannot hold: Pilot is Boat (sail or paddle type only), Jet Pack (Lemurian Squid Packs), Jet Aircraft (Lemurian only) and Submersibles (Lemurian only). Horsemanship: Serpent Hunter is not offered under Aquatic: Any."
side_effects: "Most Sea Sentinels develop a psychological need for speed and excitement. They thrive on action and are bored, fidgety and irritable when not on patrol, racing, adventuring, or engaged in rescue operations, combat, sports or some other competitive or exciting activity."
extraction_notes: |
  - Lemuria, printed 70-73 (cache p071-p074). The entry STARTS on printed 70
    and its last lines (W.P., Hand to Hand, related and secondary skills,
    equipment, cybernetics, money) are on printed 73, one page past the range
    the survey gives. Section heading: "Lemurian Men-At-Arms O.C.C.s", so
    `men_of_arms: true` and `occ_group: men-of-arms`. Every figure was checked
    against a render of the page.
  - XP ladder read off a render of printed 86, column headed "Sea Sentinel &
    Lemurian Scout": 0-2,100 / 2,101-4,200 / 4,201-8,400 / 8,401-17,200 /
    17,201-25,400 / 25,401-35,800 / 35,801-51,000 / 51,001-71,200 /
    71,201-96,400 / 96,401-131,600 / 131,601-181,800 / 181,801-232,000 /
    232,001-282,200 / 282,201-342,400 / 342,401-402,600. It must stay equal
    to the Lemurian Scout''s.
  - RACE. "Exclusive to the Lemurians, no other race is permitted" is stored
    as `race_restrictions.only: ["lemurian"]`, which assumes the Lemurian
    R.C.C. (printed 47-50) is imported under the id `lemurian`. If it lands
    under another id this line must follow it.
  - "SKILLS KNOWN BY ALL LEMURIANS" is printed inside this O.C.C.''s stat
    block with this class''s own figures (Mathematics: Basic 86%, Swimming
    76% - the Oceanic Guardsman prints 82% and 80%), so the four lines are
    stored here as O.C.C. skills. "Language: Lemurian and Oceanic at 96%"
    prints no per-level figure; +1% is the native-speaker rate on printed 55.
    "Literacy: Lemurian at 85% +1%" is granted by name as Literacy:
    Lemurian at those figures.
  - "PILOT (SPECIAL)" is printed as an O.C.C. skill line with no percentage,
    pointing at the Born to Soar ability, which gives 80% +2% per level in
    Lemurian stone vehicles. Stored as the catalog''s Symbiotic Conduit Vehicle
    Combat (printed 58, 60% +2%) at base 80, per_level 2. The O.C.C. page
    never prints that skill''s name; the pairing is the importer''s. Whether
    that skill''s own combat bonuses stack with Born to Soar''s is not stated.
  - CONDITIONAL BONUSES ARE PROSE. Born to Soar (+1 attack, +2 initiative,
    +2 automatic dodge, in Lemurian vehicles only), Machine Awareness (+1
    Perception, initiative and automatic dodge against machines) and the tech
    vehicle penalties (-15%, -1 attack) are in `special_abilities`. Stored
    bonuses are only the unconditional ones from item 6: +1 M.E., +1 P.P.,
    +2D6 S.D.C., +2 roll with impact, +1 vs Horror Factor at levels 2, 5, 7,
    9, 11, 13 and 15.
  - PSIONICS. Nine named powers, `powers_starting: 0`, no categories: "No
    other psionics are available to this character". The book prints Object
    Read; the catalog row is Object Read (Psychometry). Printed I.S.P. costs
    all match the catalog rows.
  - "AQUATIC: ANY (+5%)" names a skill group the catalog does not have as a
    category. Printed 54 lists it: Advanced Fishing, Horsemanship: Aquatic
    Animals / Sea Monsters / Serpent Hunter, Language: Cetacean / Ichthylean /
    Lemurian / Oceanic, Lore: Sea Creatures, Marine Biology, Ocean Geographic
    Surveying, Sea Holistic Medicine, Track & Hunt Sea Animals, Undersea & Sea
    Survival, Undersea Farming, Undersea Salvage and Underwater Navigation.
    Stored as one related-skills entry named Aquatic whose `only` list
    names ten of them at +5%. Marine Biology, Ocean Geographic Surveying and
    Undersea Farming are Science rows and this page prints Science: None, so
    those three are opened by name in a separate Science `only` entry at the
    same +5%; inside the Aquatic entry they would be granted but not
    takeable. Language: Lemurian, Language: Oceanic and
    Underwater Navigation are left out as O.C.C. skills of this class, and
    Horsemanship: Serpent Hunter is left out as that O.C.C.''s own skill; the
    book does not say so in as many words.
  - "Rogue: Gambling and Tailing only" is stored as Gambling (Standard) and
    Tailing; the catalog also holds Gambling (Dirty Tricks), not offered.
  - PILOT qualifiers "(Lemurian only)" and "(sail or paddle type only)" are
    in the entry''s note. Jet Pack is the row Jet Packs; Submersibles is the
    row Boat: Submersibles; Boat is the two rows Boat: Sail Type and Boat:
    Paddle Types/Canoe/Kayak.
  - EQUIPMENT. The Sea Dart Interceptor is a vehicle row
    (`lemurian-sea-dart-interceptor`), not gear, so it is a restriction line.
    "Wavestrider" is the row Wave Strider Body Armor. "One of choice"
    symbiote offers the nine non-Bio-Skin entries of printed 136-143; the
    Bio-Skins are left out because the class "has access to all Bio-Skins"
    separately. The melee pick offers every Bio-Weapon of printed 131-134
    except the two Serpent Bio-Weapons. "Short-range weapon" is not defined,
    so all ten ranged weapons of printed 134-136 are offered. Clothing is one
    row for the uniforms, dress wear and combat clothes; the water skin and
    rope print no size, so the Rifts half-gallon and 20-foot rows stand in.
    "Other common personal items" is not stored.
  - MONEY is a salary: 2,300 credits a month, one month''s pay to start,
    stored as `starting_money: 2300`. Double for squadron leaders is prose.
  - The ley line force field is stored as a trackable resource with
    `reset_on: never`: the book''s interval is six hours, which is none of
    day, session or never. Tick it by hand.
  - The book prints no P.P.E., hit point or S.D.C. base for the O.C.C.; those
    come from the Lemurian race.
