# Sea Sentinel

## Lore

The Sea Sentinels are Lemuria''s fighter pilots. They fly Stone Flyers - living stone combat vessels that move through the air like jets and through the sea like submarines - and they exist because one man, Commander Rann-gii, thought ley line energy and stone magic could be made into a small, fast fighter that might outfly the Lord of the Deep''s reaching tentacles and survive a hit or two. He built the first ones and led the force until the Lord of the Deep killed him. His pilots still carry his name: Rann-gii, or Rann-gii Flyers.

They are sworn to defend Lemuria, innocent people everywhere and the natural world, and they do it with a swagger that their commanders do not always enjoy. Sentinels are a close, proud brotherhood with a taste for speed, long odds and rescues nobody sensible would attempt, and a habit of answering a reprimand with a grin. The confidence is not empty. They handle a vessel above or below the waves as though they were made for it.

What sets them apart from other Lemurians is a feel for machines. A Sentinel senses the weapons and targeting systems turned on him, and his psionics let him climb into almost any foreign aircraft or submersible and fly it, if less gracefully than his own. That curiosity about technology worries the Biomancers, who fear it will pull the pilots away from nature and the magic of the Earth.

## GM Notes

The class leans on its vehicle. A Sentinel on foot has a light Bio-Armor, two small weapons and Hand to Hand: Basic, so plan for scenes that put the Sea Dart Interceptor (or whatever vessel the mission assigns) in play. The piloting bonuses, the halved maneuver penalties and every ley line power apply only in Lemurian stone vehicles; in a technology-based machine the pilot is at -15% and -1 attack, takes full trick maneuver penalties, and gains only a 10% speed boost on a ley line.

Machine Awareness covers one opponent at first level and one more at levels 4, 8 and 12. Its bonuses are doubled against automated attackers. The book treats the craving for speed and excitement as a penalty: a grounded Sentinel is bored, fidgety and irritable.
', 'published', 'data-script'
WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sea-sentinel');


-- Read the result back rather than trusting the exit code. d1-apply prints
-- these, and a CR in the stored markdown means the checkout mangled the file.
SELECT class_id, name, status, length(markdown) AS bytes, instr(markdown, char(13)) > 0 AS has_cr
  FROM imported_classes WHERE class_id = 'sea-sentinel';

-- Records this run. REQUIRED: the smoke test fails a data script that has no
-- footer, or whose footer names a different file.
INSERT INTO data_script_runs (filename) VALUES ('add-sea-sentinel-class.sql');
